{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-109803","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-176512","text":"Authority log retention — candidate 3 (2026-09-24)"}]},{"id":"blk-109804","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176513","text":"Branch "},{"id":"spn-176514","marks":["code"],"text":"authority-log-3"},{"id":"spn-176515","text":", on "},{"id":"spn-176516","marks":["code"],"text":"b68e6da"},{"id":"spn-176517","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-176518","marks":["code"],"text":"authority-log-closure"},{"id":"spn-176519","text":": candidate 2 "},{"id":"spn-176520","marks":["code"],"text":"91a080f"},{"id":"spn-176521","text":" + the checkpoint timings "},{"id":"spn-176522","marks":["code"],"text":"a088896"},{"id":"spn-176523","text":" + the ordered-closure fix). Human-authored infrastructure; no bot credit."}]},{"id":"blk-109805","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-176524","text":"The ruling this implements"}]},{"id":"blk-109806","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176525","text":"Travis, 2026-09-24, adopting an outside reviewer's recommendation (ProjectAmp2 "},{"id":"spn-176526","marks":["code"],"text":"SUPER_BUILDS_LANE.md"},{"id":"spn-176527","text":" §5, root commit "},{"id":"spn-176528","marks":["code"],"text":"547effd"},{"id":"spn-176529","text":"):"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-109808","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176530","text":"Retire completed items from the in-memory working lists, while preserving durable history. Keep whatever compact indexes are necessary for receipt lookup, recovery, deduplication, and preventing used grants from becoming usable again. Retirement must not remove anything an unfinished operation still needs. Verify the performance benefit after this change; bounded lists alone do not establish flat cost."}]}],"id":"blk-109807","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-109809","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176531","text":"Same day, same ruling: no install yet; a rehearsed full-world restore, not a downgrade, before any install."}]},{"id":"blk-109810","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-176532","text":"What was growing (measured on candidate 2 before this change)"}]},{"id":"blk-109811","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176533","text":"Real growth to 10,000 effects (foundation lane, "},{"id":"spn-176534","marks":["code"],"text":"3879947"},{"id":"spn-176535","text":"): tmpfs perform p50 3.9 → 6.1 ms, "},{"id":"spn-176536","marks":["bold"],"text":"p95 5.3 → 34.1 ms"},{"id":"spn-176537","text":"; the effects store handed 183 KB of state to each save at an empty journal and grew with history; every consumed one-shot grant stayed in the grant list (10,000 at the last cell). The per-save cost was the lists: "},{"id":"spn-176538","marks":["code"],"text":"Delta"},{"id":"spn-176539","text":" walks the old and new list together, appends copy the list ("},{"id":"spn-176540","marks":["code"],"text":"++"},{"id":"spn-176541","text":"), the grant view is refreshed against the whole list, the effects list is rebuilt up to the changed cell, and the log's own image holds every row too."}]},{"id":"blk-109812","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-176542","text":"The shape"}]},{"id":"blk-109813","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176543","marks":["bold"],"text":"The archive."},{"id":"spn-176544","text":" "},{"id":"spn-176545","marks":["code"],"text":"<data_dir>/authority.archive"},{"id":"spn-176546","text":", append-only, the log's frame format after its own header ("},{"id":"spn-176547","marks":["code"],"text":"AMPD-AUTHORITY-ARCHIVE/1\\n"},{"id":"spn-176548","text":"), one frame per retirement batch: "},{"id":"spn-176549","marks":["code"],"text":"%{\"b\" => n, \"rows\" => %{store => [row]}}"},{"id":"spn-176550","text":", "},{"id":"spn-176551","marks":["code"],"text":"n"},{"id":"spn-176552","text":" gapless from 1. "},{"id":"spn-176553","marks":["code"],"text":"Ampd.AuthorityLog"},{"id":"spn-176554","text":" appends and syncs a batch BEFORE the record that removes the rows from the working lists. Checkpoints never cover or delete it. Boot reads frame headers only (the last frame is verified, because a torn write can only be the last one)."}]},{"id":"blk-109814","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176555","marks":["bold"],"text":"The compact indexes"},{"id":"spn-176556","text":", in each store's own state, so they are carried by the log and its checkpoints:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-109816","spans":[{"id":"spn-176557","text":"store"}]},{"id":"blk-109817","spans":[{"id":"spn-176558","text":"field"}]},{"id":"blk-109818","spans":[{"id":"spn-176559","text":"entry"}]}],"id":"blk-109815","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-109819","spans":[{"id":"spn-176560","text":"effects"}]},{"id":"blk-109820","spans":[{"id":"spn-176561","marks":["code"],"text":"retired"}]},{"id":"blk-109821","spans":[{"id":"spn-176562","text":"id → "},{"id":"spn-176563","marks":["code"],"text":"[final_state, batch]"}]}],[{"id":"blk-109822","spans":[{"id":"spn-176564","text":"effects"}]},{"id":"blk-109823","spans":[{"id":"spn-176565","marks":["code"],"text":"retired_count"}]},{"id":"blk-109824","spans":[{"id":"spn-176566","marks":["code"],"text":"\"*\""},{"id":"spn-176567","text":" and each actor → n"}]}],[{"id":"blk-109825","spans":[{"id":"spn-176568","text":"receipts"}]},{"id":"blk-109826","spans":[{"id":"spn-176569","marks":["code"],"text":"retired_refs"}]},{"id":"blk-109827","spans":[{"id":"spn-176570","text":"effect_ref → "},{"id":"spn-176571","marks":["code"],"text":"[receipt_id, batch]"}]}],[{"id":"blk-109828","spans":[{"id":"spn-176572","text":"receipts"}]},{"id":"blk-109829","spans":[{"id":"spn-176573","marks":["code"],"text":"retired_count"}]},{"id":"blk-109830","spans":[{"id":"spn-176574","text":"kind → ("},{"id":"spn-176575","marks":["code"],"text":"\"*\""},{"id":"spn-176576","text":" and each actor → n)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-109831","spans":[{"id":"spn-176577","text":"grant_registry"}]},{"id":"blk-109832","spans":[{"id":"spn-176578","marks":["code"],"text":"retired"}]},{"id":"blk-109833","spans":[{"id":"spn-176579","text":"id → "},{"id":"spn-176580","marks":["code"],"text":"[status, batch, consumptions]"}]}],[{"id":"blk-109834","spans":[{"id":"spn-176581","text":"approvals"}]},{"id":"blk-109835","spans":[{"id":"spn-176582","marks":["code"],"text":"retired"}]},{"id":"blk-109836","spans":[{"id":"spn-176583","text":"id → "},{"id":"spn-176584","marks":["code"],"text":"[status, batch, consumed_by]"}]}],[{"id":"blk-109837","spans":[{"id":"spn-176585","text":"effects"}]},{"id":"blk-109838","spans":[{"id":"spn-176586","marks":["code"],"text":"retired_batches"}]},{"id":"blk-109839","spans":[{"id":"spn-176587","text":"batch → "},{"id":"spn-176588","marks":["code"],"text":"[lowest key, highest key, rows, %{actor => rows}]"}]}],[{"id":"blk-109840","spans":[{"id":"spn-176589","text":"receipts"}]},{"id":"blk-109841","spans":[{"id":"spn-176590","marks":["code"],"text":"retired_batches"}]},{"id":"blk-109842","spans":[{"id":"spn-176591","text":"batch → kind → the same, keyed by "},{"id":"spn-176592","marks":["code"],"text":"seq"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-109843","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176593","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-176594","marks":["code"],"text":"retired"},{"id":"spn-176595","text":" maps only ever gain keys, so "},{"id":"spn-176596","marks":["code"],"text":"Delta"},{"id":"spn-176597","text":" writes them as "},{"id":"spn-176598","marks":["code"],"text":"{:merge, store, field, added}"},{"id":"spn-176599","text":" — a new op, used for any map field that only gained keys with every old value the same term. Without it each retirement would rewrite the whole index."}]},{"id":"blk-109844","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176600","marks":["bold"],"text":"What each index answers"},{"id":"spn-176601","text":" (the ruling's four):"}]},{"id":"blk-109845","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-109847","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176602","marks":["italic"],"text":"receipt lookup"},{"id":"spn-176603","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-176604","marks":["code"],"text":"Receipts.for_effect/1"},{"id":"spn-176605","text":" falls back to "},{"id":"spn-176606","marks":["code"],"text":"retired_refs"},{"id":"spn-176607","text":" and"}]}],"id":"blk-109846","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-109848","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176608","text":"reads the row from the archive; "},{"id":"spn-176609","marks":["code"],"text":"Effects.get/1"},{"id":"spn-176610","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-176611","marks":["code"],"text":"GrantRegistry.get/1"},{"id":"spn-176612","text":" do the same by id. The archive is read by the CALLER at an offset the log hands out, never inside the registry or the log writer."}]},{"id":"blk-109849","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-109851","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176613","marks":["italic"],"text":"recovery"},{"id":"spn-176614","text":" — nothing retired is ever in flight (see below), so"}]}],"id":"blk-109850","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-109852","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176615","marks":["code"],"text":"Effects.recover!/0"},{"id":"spn-176616","text":", the recovery listing and the reconcile queue read only the working list, and lose nothing."}]},{"id":"blk-109853","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-109855","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176617","marks":["italic"],"text":"deduplication"},{"id":"spn-176618","text":" — a second receipt for a retired effect is "},{"id":"spn-176619","marks":["code"],"text":"write-duplicate"}]}],"id":"blk-109854","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-109856","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176620","text":"("},{"id":"spn-176621","marks":["code"],"text":"retired_refs"},{"id":"spn-176622","text":"); claiming a retired effect is "},{"id":"spn-176623","marks":["code"],"text":"effect-settled"},{"id":"spn-176624","text":"; moving one is "},{"id":"spn-176625","marks":["code"],"text":"journal-transition-illegal"},{"id":"spn-176626","text":" from its final state."}]},{"id":"blk-109857","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-109859","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176627","marks":["italic"],"text":"a used grant never usable again"},{"id":"spn-176628","text":" — a retired grant is not in the list the"}]}],"id":"blk-109858","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-109860","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176629","text":"decision reads, so nothing can select it; a ticket naming it is refused: "},{"id":"spn-176630","marks":["code"],"text":"write-duplicate"},{"id":"spn-176631","text":" when the ticket's effect is in the recorded consumptions (exactly what the live row would have said), "},{"id":"spn-176632","marks":["code"],"text":"write-unscoped"},{"id":"spn-176633","text":" otherwise."}]},{"id":"blk-109861","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-176634","text":"What is retired, and only together"}]},{"id":"blk-109862","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176635","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-176636","marks":["bold"],"text":"settled bundle"},{"id":"spn-176637","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-176638","marks":["code"],"text":"Ampd.Retention"},{"id":"spn-176639","text":"): an effect that is terminal ("},{"id":"spn-176640","marks":["code"],"text":"COMMITTED"},{"id":"spn-176641","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-176642","marks":["code"],"text":"FAILED"},{"id":"spn-176643","text":"), holds no live lease, is not among the newest "},{"id":"spn-176644","marks":["code"],"text":"keep_recent"},{"id":"spn-176645","text":" terminal effects, and whose recovery row — computed by "},{"id":"spn-176646","marks":["code"],"text":"Ampd.Effects.Contract.classify/3"},{"id":"spn-176647","text":", the verdict an operator's listing shows — is "},{"id":"spn-176648","marks":["code"],"text":"COMPLETE"},{"id":"spn-176649","text":", "},{"id":"spn-176650","marks":["code"],"text":"NOT_REQUIRED"},{"id":"spn-176651","text":", "},{"id":"spn-176652","marks":["code"],"text":"NOT_OWED"},{"id":"spn-176653","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-176654","marks":["code"],"text":"NOT_YET_OWED"},{"id":"spn-176655","text":" for every participant. With it: every receipt naming it; its grant iff no longer active and every consumer is retired or in the batch; its approval iff consumed by it. A row that reads "},{"id":"spn-176656","marks":["code"],"text":"MISSING"},{"id":"spn-176657","text":", "},{"id":"spn-176658","marks":["code"],"text":"CONFLICT(…)"},{"id":"spn-176659","text":", "},{"id":"spn-176660","marks":["code"],"text":"LEGACY_UNWITNESSED"},{"id":"spn-176661","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-176662","marks":["code"],"text":"INDETERMINATE"},{"id":"spn-176663","text":" is never retired — that is what an operator has to see."}]},{"id":"blk-109863","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176664","marks":["bold"],"text":"One pass is one ordered transaction and one log record"},{"id":"spn-176665","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-176666","marks":["code"],"text":"Ampd.Authority.retire_settled/1"},{"id":"spn-176667","text":" → coordinator → "},{"id":"spn-176668","marks":["code"],"text":"AuthorityLog.group/1"},{"id":"spn-176669","text":"): archive and sync the rows, then Effects, Receipts, Approvals, GrantRegistry drop and index them. That order means a refusal part-way (which the group would still commit) never leaves a live row pointing at a gone one."}]},{"id":"blk-109864","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176670","marks":["bold"],"text":"Leases."},{"id":"spn-176671","text":" Retiring an effect moves its (retired) leases out of the table the per-effect paths walk into a "},{"id":"spn-176672","marks":["code"],"text":"settled"},{"id":"spn-176673","text":" map of reason only, so a late ticket for one is still refused by its exact name ("},{"id":"spn-176674","marks":["code"],"text":"write-lease-retired"},{"id":"spn-176675","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-176676","marks":["code"],"text":"-closed"},{"id":"spn-176677","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-109865","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-176678","text":"Decisions taken as defaults (reversible; each is a setting or a line)"}]},{"id":"blk-109866","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-109868","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176679","marks":["bold"],"text":"Settings"},{"id":"spn-176680","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-176681","marks":["code"],"text":"config :ampd, authority_retention:"},{"id":"spn-176682","text":"): "},{"id":"spn-176683","marks":["code"],"text":"keep_recent"},{"id":"spn-176684","text":" 256,"}]}],"id":"blk-109867","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-109869","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176685","marks":["code"],"text":"min_batch"},{"id":"spn-176686","text":" 256, "},{"id":"spn-176687","marks":["code"],"text":"max_batch"},{"id":"spn-176688","text":" 2048, "},{"id":"spn-176689","marks":["code"],"text":"interval_ms"},{"id":"spn-176690","text":" 30,000, "},{"id":"spn-176691","marks":["code"],"text":"check_every"},{"id":"spn-176692","text":" 64, "},{"id":"spn-176693","marks":["code"],"text":"enabled"},{"id":"spn-176694","text":" true. The history windows show 50, so "},{"id":"spn-176695","marks":["code"],"text":"keep_recent"},{"id":"spn-176696","text":" ≥ 50 keeps every window's "},{"id":"spn-176697","marks":["code"],"text":"recent"},{"id":"spn-176698","text":" served from memory."}]},{"id":"blk-109870","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-109872","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176699","marks":["bold"],"text":"COMMITTED may still move"},{"id":"spn-176700","text":" to FAILED/UNKNOWN under the contract (the"}]}],"id":"blk-109871","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-109873","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176701","text":"gateway's rescue after the receipt). Retirement forecloses that move; it is safe because a live lease excludes the effect, its receipt must be COMPLETE, and the newest "},{"id":"spn-176702","marks":["code"],"text":"keep_recent"},{"id":"spn-176703","text":" are never retired — so the move can only be refused for an effect whose own perform finished long ago."}]},{"id":"blk-109874","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-109876","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176704","marks":["bold"],"text":"Archive damage does not seal authority."},{"id":"spn-176705","text":" Decisions read the indexes, not"}]}],"id":"blk-109875","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-109877","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176706","text":"the archive. A batch that does not verify on read is named in the reader's answer ("},{"id":"spn-176707","marks":["code"],"text":"archive-unreadable · …"},{"id":"spn-176708","text":"); a torn LAST batch is truncated at boot and named by a durable "},{"id":"spn-176709","marks":["code"],"text":"recovered"},{"id":"spn-176710","text":" record, like a torn log tail."}]},{"id":"blk-109878","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-109880","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176711","marks":["bold"],"text":"No witness event"},{"id":"spn-176712","text":" for a retirement: "},{"id":"spn-176713","marks":["code"],"text":"wek-r3-trace@3"},{"id":"spn-176714","text":" is WEK's format and is"}]}],"id":"blk-109879","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-109881","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176715","text":"unchanged. The retirement is the log record's ops."}]},{"id":"blk-109882","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-109884","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176716","marks":["bold"],"text":"World `schema_version` stays 3."},{"id":"spn-176717","text":" No version-3 world exists outside test"}]}],"id":"blk-109883","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":5},{"id":"blk-109885","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176718","text":"directories (candidate 2 was never installed); version 3 now means \"the log, and possibly an archive\". An installed world is version 2 and is migrated exactly as candidate 2 migrates it."}]},{"id":"blk-109886","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-109888","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176719","marks":["bold"],"text":"The trigger"},{"id":"spn-176720","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-176721","marks":["code"],"text":"Ampd.Retention"},{"id":"spn-176722","text":", a supervised process that holds no"}]}],"id":"blk-109887","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":6},{"id":"blk-109889","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176723","text":"authority: poked after each "},{"id":"spn-176724","marks":["code"],"text":"Gateway.perform"},{"id":"spn-176725","text":", looking every "},{"id":"spn-176726","marks":["code"],"text":"check_every"},{"id":"spn-176727","text":" pokes and every "},{"id":"spn-176728","marks":["code"],"text":"interval_ms"},{"id":"spn-176729","text":"; a full batch looks again at once."}]},{"id":"blk-109890","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-176730","text":"Known costs and open items"}]},{"id":"blk-109891","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-109893","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176731","marks":["bold"],"text":"Paging reads only the batches a page can reach."},{"id":"spn-176732","text":" The paged commands"}]}],"id":"blk-109892","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-109894","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176733","text":"("},{"id":"spn-176734","marks":["code"],"text":"list_effect_history"},{"id":"spn-176735","text":", "},{"id":"spn-176736","marks":["code"],"text":"list_receipts"},{"id":"spn-176737","text":") run inside the coordinator's ordered observation, so reading the whole archive there would be unbounded work in the total order. Each retired batch is indexed with its lowest and highest key and its rows per actor ("},{"id":"spn-176738","marks":["code"],"text":"retired_batches"},{"id":"spn-176739","text":"), and "},{"id":"spn-176740","marks":["code"],"text":"Projection.history_page/4"},{"id":"spn-176741","text":" reads the eligible batches newest-first, stopping once no unread batch can enter the page. A page served from the working rows reads none (tested, with the log's "},{"id":"spn-176742","marks":["code"],"text":"archive_batch_reads"},{"id":"spn-176743","text":" counter). A sparse actor's page can still read several batches — the per-actor counts skip batches with none of its rows, not batches with few."}]},{"id":"blk-109895","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-109897","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176744","marks":["bold"],"text":"A pass holds the total order"},{"id":"spn-176745","text":" for its duration (one archive sync and one"}]}],"id":"blk-109896","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-109898","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176746","text":"log record of the shrunk working lists, measured below)."}]},{"id":"blk-109899","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-109901","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176747","marks":["bold"],"text":"The compact indexes still grow with history"},{"id":"spn-176748","text":" — ~one small entry per"}]}],"id":"blk-109900","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-109902","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176749","text":"retired effect, grant and receipt, held in each registry's heap and in the log's image (and so in every checkpoint). Far smaller than the rows, but not flat: a major GC of "},{"id":"spn-176750","marks":["code"],"text":"Ampd.Effects"},{"id":"spn-176751","text":" copies its live heap, index included. If a p95 tail survives retention, this is the first suspect, and the fix is to hold the index off-heap (ETS) rather than to drop it. Per incarnation, "},{"id":"spn-176752","marks":["code"],"text":"Ampd.Effects"},{"id":"spn-176753","text":" also keeps the ticket ids of terminals and the settled leases' reasons — both compact, both reset by a restart."}]},{"id":"blk-109903","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-109905","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176754","marks":["bold"],"text":"Closure."},{"id":"spn-176755","text":" The ordered-closure gate reads CLOSED on this branch (rebased"}]}],"id":"blk-109904","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-109906","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176756","text":"onto "},{"id":"spn-176757","marks":["code"],"text":"b68e6da"},{"id":"spn-176758","text":", which closed the 15 items candidates 1 and 2 had left open and which the suite's Q.4 could not see because it reads the committed census). The archive calls cross through "},{"id":"spn-176759","marks":["code"],"text":"Ampd.Participant"},{"id":"spn-176760","text":" like every other "},{"id":"spn-176761","marks":["code"],"text":"AuthorityLog"},{"id":"spn-176762","text":" call; the regenerated census has the same crossings, opaque set and totals."}]},{"id":"blk-109907","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-109909","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176763","marks":["bold"],"text":"`approve_effect/2` on a retired approval"},{"id":"spn-176764","text":" answers "},{"id":"spn-176765","marks":["code"],"text":"approval-unknown"}]}],"id":"blk-109908","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-109910","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176766","text":"rather than "},{"id":"spn-176767","marks":["code"],"text":"approval-not-pending"},{"id":"spn-176768","text":" (it reads the working list). Both refuse."}]},{"id":"blk-109911","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-109913","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176769","marks":["bold"],"text":"The archive grows without bound"},{"id":"spn-176770","text":" — by design: the ruling is to keep"}]}],"id":"blk-109912","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-109914","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176771","text":"history. Its size and a policy for it are Travis's."}]},{"id":"blk-109915","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-109917","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176772","marks":["bold"],"text":"Directory fsync."},{"id":"spn-176773","text":" The archive's creation, like the log's rotation, does"}]}],"id":"blk-109916","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-109918","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176774","text":"not sync the directory entry; a power loss (not a process kill) right after the first batch could lose the file's name. Same gap as the log; not exercised by the kill battery, which kills processes."}]},{"id":"blk-109919","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-176775","text":"Evidence"}]},{"id":"blk-109920","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-176776","marks":["code"],"text":"evidence/retention-c3/README.md"},{"id":"spn-176777","text":": gates 9/0; full suite 1096/107 with the same 99 failing names as "},{"id":"spn-176778","marks":["code"],"text":"b68e6da"},{"id":"spn-176779","text":"; kill battery with retention active 36+36 all zeros (to 10,637 / 111,719 effects); the foundation lane's timing, OFF against ON — past 5,000 effects the tmpfs p95 goes 28.6 → 8.1 ms and ext4 88.5 → 13.9 ms, long GCs to zero, VM 668 → 247 MB, boot at 10k 660 → 101 ms. The costs it leaves: archived by-id reads are O(batch) (~6.6 ms each), and the retired indexes grow (AuthorityLog 9.6 → 20.7 MB from 500 to 10k). The restore rehearsal: ProjectAmp2 "},{"id":"spn-176780","marks":["code"],"text":"superlane/restore-rehearsal/"},{"id":"spn-176781","text":"."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierazqmasgjfgxbujhi27iogor2i2rrbczwopm3juz57x3ebilhuvz4a","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}